Settings
  every setting, its default, what it takes, and how to change it

What it is

  A setting is a named switch, like `theme` or `gatePrompt`. Each one has a
  default, and you only write the ones you want different.

  The settings come in groups:

  - Appearance: theme, density, animations, statusBar, colorMode
  - Models & roles: continueOnSubscription, subscriptionOrder,
    continueOnAPIModel
  - Interaction: composer, gatePrompt, gateAskWaitSeconds, gateAskTimeout,
    askPersonWaitSeconds, readBeforeEdit, autoUpdate
  - Context: chatShowsTools, agentFeeds, showThinking, thinkingSummary, images,
    projectInstructionsCap, contextCeiling, instructionSources, skills, memory,
    autoMemory, episodes, memoryFromAllUsers, memoryModel, learn
  - Files: diffContext, hyperlinks, groupByAgent
  - Shell: persistentRegistry, logTail, killConfirm, shell, foldHidesShell
  - Turn: decisionCap, turnMaySpawn, oneWorkingSessionPerProject, planEveryStep,
    sideChatAccess, subAgentsPerTurn, subAgentDepth, leadCache, subAgentCache,
    subAgentCheckSeconds, subAgentWatchSeconds, verifySubAgents, agentSources,
    modelTier.genius, modelTier.smart, modelTier.worker, modelTier.dumb
  - Projects: projectManagement (boardy, the ticket board), boardFlow (the words
    boardy uses), scratchCleanupDays and scratchMaxGB (the scratchpad)
  - Browser: browser, browserDriver, browserSteps, browserModel, browserEffort,
    browserCursor, browserProfile, browserHeadless

  `gatePrompt` is `auto` by default, which is auto mode: Jev decides at every
  gate and the work does not stop for you. Only a call it denies is refused, and
  the model is told why. A call it would ask about runs, and shows in the chat
  with its verdict. Every decision is a ledger row `tofu why` reads. `tofu
  settings set gatePrompt ask` turns asking on: a call Jev would ask about waits
  for your answer, `1` to allow it once, `2` to deny it, `3` to allow it here
  from now on. A project hook that asks, a rule override and the model changing
  a setting ask you in both modes: no classifier answers the first two, and the
  last could otherwise turn its own gate off. `tofu run` has nobody to ask, so
  there an ask is refused in both modes.

  `leadCache` is how long the lead's prompt cache lives on a subscription, `1h`
  by default. `5m` writes the whole cache at the cheaper five minute rate, and a
  pause past five minutes then writes it again. `history-5m` keeps the tools and
  system prompt an hour and writes the conversation at five minutes, so a pause
  rewrites only the conversation. `subAgentCache` is the same choice for a
  sub-agent, `1h` or `5m`. `tofu session trace` shows each request's write at
  the lifetime it got.

  `continueOnSubscription`, `subscriptionOrder` and `continueOnAPIModel` say
  where work goes when every account of a subscription is at its limit: a model
  on another subscription, in that order, then one paid by your key. With none
  set the work stops and names them. `tofu docs usage` has more.

  A setting changed in one window, by `tofu settings set` or by hand, reaches
  every open window and the project's host on the next turn, with no reload.

The detail

  Each setting's own line is two sentences at most. The rest is here.

  - `continueOnSubscription`: when every account on the subscription a turn or a
    sub-agent runs on is at its limit, it continues on the model picked here for
    another subscription provider, one model per provider, the first in
    `subscriptionOrder` with an account left. Shown, with `subscriptionOrder`,
    when you have accounts on more than one subscription provider. Empty
    `subscriptionOrder` tries providers in the order they were picked.
  - `continueOnAPIModel`: used by a turn or a sub-agent once no subscription has
    an account left.
  - `gatePrompt`: under `auto`, only what Jev denies is refused, and what it
    would ask about runs and shows its verdict in the chat. Under `ask`, a call
    waits until you answer or `gateAskWaitSeconds` passes.
  - `gateAskWaitSeconds`: applies under `auto` and `ask` alike. A cron job that
    fires while a call waits decides it at once. The next ask reads the new
    value.
  - `gateAskTimeout`: a call only you may allow changes settings, hooks or the
    harness, which is why `refuse` is the default.
  - `askPersonWaitSeconds`: the question stays open and a later answer still
    reaches the lead. Under `ask` the lead waits with no timeout. The next turn
    reads the new value.
  - `autoUpdate`: the lookup runs at most once an hour. With it off, `tofu
    update` installs the release. A build from source never updates.
  - `thinkingSummary`: `omitted` means no thinking reaches the sub-agents feed.
  - `contextCeiling`: a model whose window is smaller stops at its window less
    the answer's reserve. `TOFU_CONTEXT_CEILING` and `--context-ceiling` win
    over it, and the next turn reads the new value.
  - `instructionSources`: `agents-first` sends AGENTS.md and `claude-first`
    sends CLAUDE.md. They are read from the working directory up to its git
    root, and the home directory gives only `~/.tofu/AGENTS.md`.
  - `skills`: the skill folders are `.tofu`, `.agents` and `.claude` in the
    project, and only `~/.tofu/skills` in the home directory.
  - `memory`: on also lets the lead offer one short rule. `tofu memory` lists
    the entries.
  - `autoMemory`: answering always on a memory card turns it on.
  - `episodes`: on also sends their view after the memory and through every
    fork, and offers zoom and recall. Off keeps none and offers neither, while
    the memory still goes.
  - `memoryFromAllUsers`: the memory lives in the repository's `.tofu` folder.
    Project local memory applies to everyone either way.
  - `memoryModel`: each summary is one line of at most 512 bytes. Empty takes
    the model the library marks `memory: yes` for the session's own source,
    never the OpenRouter key.
  - `learn`: it prints how many windows and bytes it sends first, and writes
    each proposal with your lead model.
  - `persistentRegistry`: off stops every shell on exit, even when tofu is
    killed. Read on the next start.
  - `shell`: one of the offered values or a path to a shell. Empty resolves the
    person's own shell.
  - `planEveryStep`: each sub-agent keeps a plan of its own and sees that one.
    The next turn reads the new value.
  - `sideChatAccess`: `read` writes nothing, `notes` writes .md and .html files,
    `files` writes anywhere, and any other value is a comma list of globs. A
    side chat never spawns, schedules, remembers or changes a setting, whatever
    this says.
  - `subAgentsPerTurn`, `subAgentDepth`, `subAgentCache` and
    `subAgentCheckSeconds`: the next spawn reads the new value.
  - `subAgentCheckSeconds`: the check is built from what tofu records: the
    sub-agent's steps, the files it changed, its gate and its last tool.
  - `subAgentWatchSeconds`: the chat line says what the call is doing, such as
    waiting for the orchestrator's answer, running bash or building. A sub-agent
    with no new output, step or request for this long is stalled.
  - `verifySubAgents`: the lead reads what the sub-agent changed, runs the build
    or the tests again and opens what it made. Off takes the report as the
    result unless you ask for a check. `tofu rules off verify_sub_agents` turns
    it off too, whatever this says.
  - `agentSources`: a comma list, inside the project. The home directory gives
    only `~/.tofu/agents`, and the library is always read.
  - `projectManagement`: a spawn names a ticket, its owns become the sub-agent's
    paths and the sub-agent moves it to review.
  - `boardFlow`: jira says ticket, board, epic, sprint and points. linear says
    issue, team, project, cycle and estimate.
  - `scratchCleanupDays`: only a folder with no tofu running it is deleted, its
    processes stopped first.
  - `sessionStaleDays`: no activity means no new event, request or open. The
    deletion runs when the project's host starts or on `tofu session clean`. A
    session a kept one continues or branches from, the head, one open now and
    one with a live cron job are kept.
  - `browserDriver`: `subagent` hands the steps to a browser sub-agent on
    `browserModel`, spawned with a task and a tab. `steps` gives the model
    `browser_observe` and `browser_act`. `goal` gives it `browser_do`, where Jev
    picks each step toward a whole goal.
  - `browserModel`: a subscription model. Empty takes the dumb tier, then the
    worker tier, then the turn's own model.
  - `browserEffort`: used when the model lists effort. The model's own default
    is the lowest it lists at or above low.
  - `browserCursor`: it never changes what tofu reads or clicks, and is read
    when Chrome starts the relay.
  - `browserProfile`: tofu starts the installed Chrome on that profile's own
    folder under the tofu home, so a site signed in once with `tofu browser
    profile login` stays signed in.
  - `browserHeadless`: read when that Chrome starts, and never by your own
    Chrome.

Where it lives

  - `~/.tofu/settings.json`: yours, in every project
  - `.tofu/settings.json` in a project: that project only

  The project file wins over yours, and yours wins over the default.

Change it

      tofu settings set <key> <value>

  writes your file. Add `--scope project` to write the project's instead:

      tofu settings set --scope project gatePrompt ask

  A true or false setting takes `true` or `false`. A list takes commas and no
  spaces, like `tofu,claude`. A value the setting does not take is refused and
  nothing is written. An older value a setting used to take, like
  `AGENTS.md,CLAUDE.md` for `instructionSources`, is read and written as the
  choice it became. In the app, type `/settings` for the same list with a
  search.

  A setting marked (on the next start) is read once when tofu opens, so quit and
  open it again.

Check it

      tofu settings

  prints every setting by group, its value, and `project`, `global` or `default`
  for where it came from, with `●` on the ones you set.

      tofu settings get <key>

  prints one value. Both take `--json` and print one JSON document. `set` prints
  one `~` line with the file and `→ undo:` with the command that puts the old
  value back.

Undo it

  Set it back to the default shown below, or delete its line from the settings
  file. With the line gone, the next file down wins.

Every setting

Appearance
    theme                        tofu
      one of tofu, tofu light, tofu dusk, Solarized Light, Dracula, Nord,
      Gruvbox, terminal
      tofu uses Zed Nu Disco; choose a palette
    density                      comfortable
      one of compact, comfortable, spacious
      Spacing across lists and panels
    animations                   subtle
      one of off, subtle, full
      Motion for conversational states
    statusBar                    compact
      one of compact, detailed, hidden
      Context, quotas, and runtime counters
    colorMode                    auto
      one of auto, truecolor, 256 colors, ANSI 16
      Terminal color capability

Models & roles
    continueOnSubscription       empty
      any text
      Where work continues, on another subscription, once every account on this
      one is at its limit. Empty stops it
    subscriptionOrder            empty
      a comma list of claude-sub, codex-sub
      The order continueOnSubscription tries providers in, as a comma list of
      sources. Empty keeps the order picked
    continueOnAPIModel           empty
      any text
      The model, paid by its key, that work continues on when no subscription
      has an account left. Empty stops it

Interaction
    composer                     standard
      one of standard, compact, expanded
      Enter sends; Shift+Enter inserts a line break
    gatePrompt                   auto
      one of auto, ask
      auto lets Jev decide at every gate, so work never stops for you. ask waits
      for you on what Jev would ask about
    gateAskWaitSeconds           180
      at least 1 seconds an ask waits for you
      Seconds a gate ask waits for your answer before gateAskTimeout decides it
    gateAskTimeout               refuse
      one of refuse, allow
      What an ask nobody answered in time does. refuse turns it down and tells
      the lead why, allow runs it
    askPersonWaitSeconds         120
      at least 1 seconds before the recommended option is taken under auto
      Under auto, seconds before a question the lead asks you takes its
      recommended option
    readBeforeEdit               true
      true or false
      an edit or a write to a file this session has not read, or that changed
      since it was read, is refused
    autoUpdate                   true
      true or false
      on installs a newer release in the background for the next start. off only
      says one is out

Context
    chatShowsTools               false
      true or false
      chat shows every tool call
    agentFeeds                   full
      one of full, summary, off
      full keeps every sub-agents event, summary the latest 200, off shows only
      the list of agents
    showThinking                 true
      true or false
      thinking shows in each agent's sub-agents feed; t there toggles it
    thinkingSummary              summarized
      one of summarized, omitted
      summarized asks Claude for a summary of its thinking. omitted asks for
      none
    images                       auto
      one of auto, inline, off
      auto sends a pasted image only to a model that can see, inline always
      sends, off never attaches
    projectInstructionsCap       32768
      1 to 262144 bytes of AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md sent each turn
      bytes of your instruction files sent each turn
    contextCeiling               450000
      at least 1 tokens a request may carry
      The most tokens one request may carry. The conversation forks before it
    instructionSources           agents-first
      one of agents-first, claude-first, both
      Which of AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md a folder with both sends. both sends both
      and costs more tokens
    skills                       on
      one of on, off
      on lists your skills to the model and offers the skill tool. off sends
      neither
    memory                       true
      true or false
      on sends what you asked tofu to remember on every request. off sends none
    autoMemory                   false
      true or false
      on keeps a rule the lead offers at once and prints the undo, instead of
      asking first
    episodes                     on
      one of on, off
      on keeps this project's conversation as episodes and sends their view.
      Needs memory on
    memoryFromAllUsers           off
      one of on, off
      on applies the user local memory every author kept in this repository. off
      applies only yours
    memoryModel                  empty
      any text
      The model that writes memory summaries, as source/model. Empty takes the
      library's memory model
    learn                        false
      true or false
      on lets tofu learn send windows of your messages to Jev for labels. off
      runs it on this machine only

Files
    diffContext                  3
      one of 2, 3, 5, 8
      Lines around changed hunks, at most the 3 each diff carries
    hyperlinks                   auto
      one of auto, on, off
      OSC 8 terminal file links; off prints the bare path
    groupByAgent                 true
      true or false
      Author filters in edit feeds

Shell
    persistentRegistry           false               on the next start
      true or false
      A running shell outlives tofu and the next launch lists it. off stops
      every shell on exit
    logTail                      500
      one of 100, 500, 1000
      Lines retained per shell
    killConfirm                  true
      true or false
      Confirm process termination
    shell                        empty
      any text
      The shell commands run in: wsl or a path. Empty finds your own shell
    foldHidesShell               false
      true or false
      the running line drops the shell count

Turn
    decisionCap                  0
      0 to 1000 decisions a turn, where 0 means no cap
      decision cap per turn, zero means no cap
    turnMaySpawn                 true
      true or false
      a turn may spawn a sub-agent
    oneWorkingSessionPerProject  true
      true or false
      While one session in this project works, any other waits. off lets several
      work at once
    planEveryStep                true
      true or false
      The lead sees its plan and each step's status before every step. off shows
      it only on the plan tool
    sideChatAccess               read
      any text
      What a new side chat may write: read, notes for .md and .html, files for
      anywhere, or a comma list of globs
    subAgentsPerTurn             10
      at least 1 sub-agents running at once
      How many sub-agents may run at once. A spawn past it is refused until one
      ends
    subAgentDepth                2
      at least 1 levels of sub-agents
      How deep a sub-agent may spawn its own sub-agents
    leadCache                    1h
      one of 1h, 5m, history-5m
      How long the lead's prompt cache lives on a subscription. 5m costs less,
      1h lasts, history-5m mixes them
    subAgentCache                1h
      one of 1h, 5m
      How long a sub-agent's prompt cache lives. 5m writes cost less, 1h writes
      last an hour
    subAgentCheckSeconds         1800
      at least 0 seconds between checks on a running sub-agent, where 0 sends
      none
      Seconds between the lead's checks on each running sub-agent, made with no
      model call. 0 sends none
    subAgentWatchSeconds         600
      at least 1 seconds before a long call is named, and before a sub-agent
      with no progress is stalled
      Seconds before a long sub-agent call is named in the chat, and a sub-agent
      with no progress shows stalled
    verifySubAgents              true
      true or false
      The lead checks each sub-agent's work itself before it reports. off takes
